<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ganga Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1880">1880</a>–<a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ganga Singh was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Bikaner from 1887 to 1943 and one of the most prominent Indian princes of his time. He modernised his desert state, built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gang-canal">Gang Canal</a> to irrigate its north and expanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganga-risala">Ganga Risala</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camel</a> corps. He sat in the Imperial War Cabinet during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and was the first chancellor of the Chamber of Princes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ganga-singh.jpg" alt="Ganga Singh" width="320" height="486" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Vandyk · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ganga_Singh_c1930.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
